  body: "# State Pension: the post-2016 regime in the DMG\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe captured guide uses
    SP for the legislative State Pension regime and contrasts it with RP, the old State Pension regime, using the
    date pensionable age is reached as the introductory boundary.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe introduction
    uses 6 April 2016 as a regime boundary; it is not a standalone eligibility test or a statement of the current
    pensionable age. Transitional, inherited and pension-sharing provisions have their own conditions. Pension Credit
    and Universal Credit are separate benefits.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 74001, PDF page 1](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=1).\n\
    - [DMG 74003, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=2).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch74` — PDF SHA-256 `5961a9cb7c86814a0f6fa147c0a8a551b4258c803680fac14a95cab9eca1afd6`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `c762e93940b4342d70d5bc96a80c3e094c91852d93868f5709e04f293faef61a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/rp-old-pension-regime
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source expressly distinguishes the SP and RP labels and directs readers to chapter 75 for
      RP; skos:related is not equivalence.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0001
      quote: "74001 This Chapter gives guidance on SP. SP is the legislative term for “new state pension” whereas
        the\nlegislative term for “old state pension” is RP. To be entitled to SP, a person must reach pensionable
        age\n\non or after 6.4.161. A person who reached pensionable age before 6.4.16 may be entitled to RP 2.\n\
        \n\nNote: See DMG Chapter 75 for guidance on RP.\n\n\n                                                 \
        \                 1 Pensions Act 14, s 1(2); 2 SS CB Act 92"
      locator: DMG 74001
  - target: term/sp-transitional-rate
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source identifies a transitional rate among the SP routes without saying every claimant
      uses the same calculation.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0003
      quote: "74011 Entitlement to SP may be at\n\n\n1. the full rate (see DMG 74101 et seq) or\n\n\n2. the reduced
        rate (see DMG 74151 et seq) or\n\n\n3. the transitional rate (see DMG 74201 et seq).\n\n\nNote: Entitlement
        to SP may be postponed or suspended (see DMG 74501 et seq)."
      locator: DMG 74011
